Congratulations for trying to understand this! I can't locate the exact equation you cite in the 2009 paper, but note that the compact description there is for a homogeneous model (i.e. activity centres uniformly distributed in the plane, no weighting for varying density). See Borchers & Efford (2008) for the inhomogeneous (varying density) case. The denominator is the effective sampling area a rather than a probability.
Yes, it's integrating over all positions, but that bypasses the need to infer the actual location.

