Your original summary showed one session, but now you imply six? Does it work without telemetry? Does it work with telemetry alone? NA values indicate that the model did not fit for which there are several possible explanations. See, for example, the troubleshooting appendix in the SECR book. That does not deal with telemetry, but it may give hints. One is to try starting values based on the non-telemetry data. Sometimes adding telemetry just doesn't work because of incompatibility with the capture data or telemetry overpowers the more important capture-recapture component.
Are you sure that telemetry adds significantly to the capture-recapture analysis?

I remain sceptical.

